  "ingredients": [
    "2 (8 ounce) sweet potatoes",
    "1 egg",
    "1 clove garlic, pressed",
    "0.5 teaspoon salt",
    "0.5 teaspoon ground nutmeg",
    "2 cups all-purpose flour"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake sweet potatoes in the preheated oven until soft to the touch, about 30 minutes. Remove from the oven and let cool, 15 to 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove and discard skins from cooled potatoes. Mash flesh in a large bowl or press through a ricer. Blend in egg, garlic, salt, and nutmeg. Mix in flour, a little at a time, until a soft dough forms.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "While the water is coming to a boil, make the gnocchi: Roll dough on a floured surface into several long, snake-like logs. Cut logs into 1-inch pieces.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Drop dough pieces into boiling water and cook until they float to the surface. Transfer with a slotted spoon to a serving dish and keep warm until ready to serve.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    }
  ],
